S6: the readable assertion the ruling asked for, and what it reads.

ab124a00e -- `Variant::updateRefs` now answers "how does the trace know this value's type" with the
type pointer it was handed (the type travels down the scan from the slot the value was found in:
mm/gen.cpp TraceEntry / RefTraceInfo), and stops with a report instead of faulting. It stays in
release on purpose: ASSERT is ((void)0) under NDEBUG, which is why this path died with exit 139 and
no word. CAMEL_TRACE_VARIANT=1 prints the reading per relocated value, before the type is read.

The reading, on mlp + std::macro std::defunctionalize std::nvm with the training workload:
  [variant] trace value=0x7cf65c2ffdd8 type=0x7cf657c3be30 tag=0 fields=1
  [variant] the reference trace cannot use the type of a Variant: the type it was traced with has
            code 1610612746, which is not an enum's
  [variant]   the type reads as: (x: f32[..]) => float
1610612746 = 0x6000000A = TypeCode::Function. So none of the three guessed shapes: no type id (the
scan carries a pointer), no bad tag (tag 0, one field, a well-formed Variant), no dangling pointer
(the pointer reads back as a well-formed function type). The value became the enum and was written
into a slot still typed as the function it used to be: the representation conversion was done on the
value and not on the position.

